{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CREATE AN ACCOUNT — /account/register

   Two steps on one route: a chooser, then the individual form
   (`?as=individual`).

   ── WHY A CHOOSER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Four kinds of account exist on this platform and until now exactly one of
   them was reachable from the public site. Somebody nominated by a friend, a
   non-profit that wants a Giving page, a trader after a stand: each had a
   route, a form and a controller, and no door anybody could find. The
   organisation application was linked from the ORGANISATION SIGN-IN — a page
   you reach by already having an account. That is this codebase's oldest
   shape of fault: a mechanism complete on every side with no way in.

   Every row below goes somewhere that exists. No row is aspirational.

   ── THE ERROR PATH RETURNS TO THE FORM, NOT TO STEP ONE ────────────────────
   `registerSubmit` redirects back to `?as=individual` on a validation failure.
   Dropping somebody on the chooser instead would show them four options and
   no sign of the message explaining what was wrong with what they typed.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% extends "layout/account-auth.twig" %}

{% block card %}
{% if as|default('') == 'individual' %}

  <a class="ag-acct__back" href="/account/register">
    <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12.5 4.5 7 10l5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    Back
  </a>

  <h1 class="ag-acct__h1">Create your account</h1>
  <p class="ag-acct__lede">Free, takes a minute. A password is optional — you can always sign in with an email code.</p>

  {% if error %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--err" role="alert">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}

  {# ── THE RULES THE SERVER ENFORCES, SAID BEFORE IT ENFORCES THEM ──────────
     `UserAccountService::register()` refuses a one-word name, a disposable inbox and a
     password under eight characters. Every one of those was a round trip that came back
     as a red sentence, and the disposable rule in particular reads as arbitrary when you
     meet it for the first time in a refusal — the page had never said addresses are
     checked, so the only way to learn it was to be turned away.

     The branch beside this one states its requirements above its first field for exactly
     this reason. Same here. A `pattern` and a `minlength` catch the first and the third
     where the person who typed them is still standing there; the second cannot be checked
     in a browser, so it is said instead. #}

  <form method="post" action="/account/register">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    {# The member branch, named in the BODY as the organisation one is. It was implicit —
       anything without `as=organisation` fell through to here — which works and reads as
       an accident waiting for a third branch. #}
    <input type="hidden" name="as" value="individual">

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="name">Full name</label>
      {# Two words, because that is the server's rule. Spelled as a pattern rather than
         left to the round trip — and `title` carries the reason, which is what a browser
         shows when it refuses. #}
      <input class="ag-acct__input" id="name" type="text" name="name" value="{{ old.name|default('') }}"
             autocomplete="name" placeholder="First and last name" required autofocus
             pattern="\s*\S+\s+.*\S.*" title="First and last name, please — both.">
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="email">Email</label>
      {# The one failure that has a field to blame: an address already in use. #}
      <input class="ag-acct__input{% if error %} ag-acct__input--err{% endif %}" id="email" type="email" name="email"
             value="{{ old.email|default('') }}" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required>
      <small class="ag-acct__hint">Where your vote receipts and tickets go, so it has to be
        one you keep — disposable inboxes are refused.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      {# Required, and that is current behaviour rather than an oversight —
         vote receipts and event tickets reach people by phone. #}
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="phone">Phone</label>
      <input class="ag-acct__input" id="phone" type="tel" name="phone" value="{{ old.phone|default('') }}"
             autocomplete="tel" inputmode="tel" placeholder="+234…" required>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="password">Password <span>optional</span></label>
      {# `minlength`, which this field did not carry. The eight was in the PLACEHOLDER — a
         string that vanishes the moment somebody types, so the only person who ever saw
         the rule was one who had not started, and the only one who needed it was one who
         had. The server has always enforced it. #}
      <input class="ag-acct__input" id="password" type="password" name="password"
             minlength="8" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="At least 8 characters">
      <small class="ag-acct__hint">Leave it blank and we email you a one-time code each time
        you sign in. You can set one later either way.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__btns">
      <button class="ag-acct__cta" type="submit">Create account</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <p class="ag-acct__fine">We email you a link to confirm the address before the account is
    usable. By continuing you accept the <a href="/terms">Terms</a> and
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a>.</p>

{% elseif as|default('') == 'organisation' %}

  {# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     REGISTER AN ORGANISATION — the second branch of the one door.

     This was `/giving/apply`: its own route, its own controller and a 403-line
     page of its own. Every word here that explains a requirement is carried over
     from it deliberately — that page's docblock says an application form which
     hides its requirements "wastes the time of the people least able to spare
     it", and moving a form is the commonest way that kind of copy gets dropped.

     ── GROUPED, NOT STEPPED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Ten fields in a 452px card is a wall. The obvious answer is a wizard, and it
     is the wrong one here: a stepped form needs script to move between steps, and
     an applicant whose browser blocks it gets a first step and no second. Three
     labelled groups in one form read as three short asks, submit in one post, and
     work with nothing running.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

  <a class="ag-acct__back" href="/account/register">
    <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12.5 4.5 7 10l5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    Back
  </a>

  <h1 class="ag-acct__h1">Register your organisation</h1>
  <p class="ag-acct__lede">Raise through Giving, with the money settled straight into your own
    account — it never passes through Africa GATES.</p>

  {% if error %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--err" role="alert">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}

  {% if org_signed_in|default(false) %}
    {# The apply page refused this on POST only, so the form still drew for somebody who
       already had an organisation — and the refusal arrived after they had filled it in. #}
    <div class="ag-acct__alert" role="status">
      You are already signed in as an organisation. <a href="/org">Continue from your
      dashboard</a> — registering again would create a second record for the same body,
      and a reviewer would have to work out which of the two is real.
    </div>
  {% else %}

  {# Said before the first field rather than after the last: these are the two documents
     without which nothing can be approved, and somebody who does not have them should
     find that out now rather than after typing for ten minutes. #}
  <ul class="ag-acct__reqs">
    <li><b>CAC registration</b> — only an incorporated body may collect charitable gifts in
      Nigeria. Incorporated Trustees numbers begin <b>IT</b>; an RC or BN is accepted and
      noted for the reviewer.</li>
    <li><b>SCUML registration</b> — you can apply without the number. You cannot be approved
      without it.</li>
    <li><b>A settlement account in your registered name</b>, checked with your bank before
      anything is paid.</li>
  </ul>

  <form method="post" action="/account/register" class="ag-acct__form">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    {# The branch travels in the BODY. A submit does not carry the query string, so a
       controller forking on `?as=` would send every organisation down the member path. #}
    <input type="hidden" name="as" value="organisation">

    <fieldset class="ag-acct__group">
      <legend class="ag-acct__legend">Your organisation</legend>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgName">Name supporters will know you by</label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgName" type="text" name="name" maxlength="200" required autofocus
               value="{{ old.name|default('') }}" placeholder="Bright Futures Initiative">
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">This appears on your donation page.</small>
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgLegal">Registered name at the CAC</label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgLegal" type="text" name="legal_name" maxlength="200" required
               value="{{ old.legal_name|default('') }}">
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">Exactly as registered, including the spelling — it is
          compared against the name your bank returns for your account.</small>
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgCac">CAC number</label>
        {# The pattern catches the gross shape in the browser, where the person who made the
           typo is still standing there. Deliberately looser than the server's rule: a
           browser that silently refuses a real number teaches nothing, while the server's
           refusal names the three prefixes and can be read. #}
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgCac" type="text" name="cac_number" maxlength="60" required
               value="{{ old.cac_number|default('') }}" placeholder="IT/1234567"
               autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false"
               pattern="[A-Za-z]{2}[ /-]*[0-9]{1,10}"
               title="Two letters — RC, BN or IT — then the digits. For example IT/1234567.">
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgScuml">SCUML number <span>if you have it yet</span></label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgScuml" type="text" name="scuml_number" maxlength="60"
               value="{{ old.scuml_number|default('') }}">
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="ag-acct__group">
      <legend class="ag-acct__legend">Your sign-in</legend>
      <p class="ag-acct__note">This creates an account as well as an application — one step,
        not two, because an account belonging to somebody who never finished applying is a
        row nobody reviews and nobody deletes.</p>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgEmail">Email</label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input{% if error %} ag-acct__input--err{% endif %}" id="orgEmail"
               type="email" name="contact_email" maxlength="190" required autocomplete="email"
               value="{{ old.contact_email|default('') }}" placeholder="you@organisation.org">
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">This becomes your sign-in, and it is where the decision goes.</small>
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgPass">Choose a password</label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgPass" type="password" name="password"
               minlength="12" required autocomplete="new-password">
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">At least 12 characters. This sign-in can later request
          payouts, so it is held to a higher bar than a shopping account.</small>
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgContact">Contact name <span>optional</span></label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgContact" type="text" name="contact_name" maxlength="160"
               autocomplete="name" value="{{ old.contact_name|default('') }}">
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">Who a reviewer should write to, if that is somebody other than you.</small>
      </div>

      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgPhone">Phone <span>optional</span></label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="orgPhone" type="tel" name="contact_phone" maxlength="40"
               autocomplete="tel" inputmode="tel" value="{{ old.contact_phone|default('') }}">
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="ag-acct__group">
      <legend class="ag-acct__legend">What you do</legend>
      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="orgWhat">In your own words</label>
        <textarea class="ag-acct__input ag-acct__input--area" id="orgWhat" name="description" rows="5"
          placeholder="Who you work with, where, and what a donation actually pays for.">{{ old.description|default('') }}</textarea>
        <small class="ag-acct__hint">This is what a reviewer reads first, and what supporters
          read on your page. Plain sentences beat a mission statement.</small>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    {# What pressing it does, before it is pressed. Carried from the apply page, where it
       was four numbered steps under the button. #}
    <ol class="ag-acct__next">
      <li>Your account is created and you are signed in. The record lands as a draft and
        nothing about your organisation is public.</li>
      <li>You upload your certificates on your own dashboard. Nothing can be reviewed until
        they are on file.</li>
      <li>Your CAC number is checked against the register, in the background, so it costs you
        no waiting.</li>
      <li>You hear either way, <b>with a reason</b>.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="ag-acct__btns">
      <button class="ag-acct__cta" type="submit">Send application</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <p class="ag-acct__fine"><b>Free.</b> This takes no payment and asks for no card details.
    Looking to trade at an event rather than raise donations?
    <a href="/events">Apply for a stand</a> instead.</p>
  {% endif %}

{% else %}

  <h1 class="ag-acct__h1">Join Africa GATES</h1>
  <p class="ag-acct__lede">Pick where to start. You can add the others later without a second account.</p>

  {% if error %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--err" role="alert">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}

  <div class="ag-acct__rows">
    <a class="ag-acct__row ag-acct__row--tall" href="/account/register?as=individual">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Take part</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Earn points, vote in categories and nominate people.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
    <a class="ag-acct__row ag-acct__row--tall" href="/vote">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Claim your profile</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Someone nominated you. Open your page, verify by code, and it is yours to edit.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
    <a class="ag-acct__row ag-acct__row--tall" href="/account/register?as=organisation">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Register a non-profit</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Raise through Giving, with the money paid to your own account. CAC and SCUML registration required.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
    <a class="ag-acct__row ag-acct__row--tall" href="/partner">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Partner or exhibit</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Sponsor a programme, take a stand at an event, or list in the shop.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
  </div>

{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block below %}
<p class="ag-acct__switch">Already a member? <a class="ag-acct__quiet" href="/account/login">Sign in</a></p>
{% endblock %}
